# deps / build
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
coverage/
# env / secrets — NEVER commit
.env
.env.local
*.client_secret.json
token.json
# local personal data — never commit real ledgers
data/ledgers/*.json
data/ledgers/*.csv
!data/ledgers/*.example.json
!data/ledgers/.gitkeep
# os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.log
# a local developer-machine convenience script: it nudges the mouse pointer to keep a workstation
# awake. It holds no project role, is imported by nothing, and belongs to whoever is sitting at the
# machine — not to the build. Ignored rather than tracked so it stops failing AC14 (clean tree).
jiggle.ps1
# the same script, rewritten. `awake.ps1` supersedes `jiggle.ps1`, `awake.cmd` is the shortcut that
# launches it, and `_archive/` holds the two earlier drafts (`awake.v1.ps1`, `awake.v2.ps1`) that
# their author kept rather than discarded. Same reasoning as above and for the same reason: they
# nudge the pointer on one workstation, nothing in the build imports them, and they carry no
# deployment particular and no secret. Ignored rather than tracked so they stop failing AC14
# (clean tree). Deliberately NOT deleted — superseded or not, they belong to whoever is sitting at
# the machine, and a build gate is not a licence to remove another person's local tooling.
awake.ps1
awake.cmd
_archive/
# continuation analysis + build session inputs (tooling, not app code)
outputs/
Execute and build.md
# loop scratch (the ledger itself IS committed)
.loop/tmp/
# benchmark run outputs (contract 09's five artifacts). Regenerable from tracked inputs — the eval
# set, the recorded fixture and src/server/benchmark — and a PROVISIONAL registry emitted from
# fixtures must not sit in a public repository looking like graded evidence. Phase 6.3 replaces it
# with a live-measured one, which is likewise a run output rather than source.
artifacts/
# raw third-party API dumps captured by research tooling: regenerable by the scripts beside them,
# and they carry third-party prose that the generic-only check (AC11) forbids in a tracked file.
docs/research/**/_raw/
# an IN-FLIGHT research run. Its report, shortlist, exclusions and integration notes are still being
# authored and rewritten as its tooling fetches primary sources, so the folder is a staging area, not
# a deliverable. Ignored so the acceptance gate is not measuring another process's scratch space.
# Track it (and restore the _RESEARCH_INDEX.md row) once the run is finished and its author says so.
docs/research/2026-08-07-oss-design-scan/
# --- local secrets (never commit) ---
.secrets/
.env.*.local
*client_secret*.json
secretsgoogle*.txt
# A FILLED-IN container env file. `ops/env/*.env.example` are the tracked templates, but a real
# `ops/env/<name>.env` holds live bot tokens and API keys. The `.env` rule above matches only a
# file named exactly ".env", so `ops/env/proxy.env` was NOT ignored: proven with
# `git check-ignore -v` on 2026-08-09, on a PUBLIC repository. The `.example` templates are
# unaffected because they do not end in `.env`.
ops/env/*.env
# any Cloudflare API token file, wherever it lands
*cloudflare*.env
cf_token*

# The SEEDED SERVER STORE. Spec 08 wave A2 materialises the owner's real ledger into a local SQLite
# file so waves A3 and A4 can reconcile and index against it, and wave A5 moves it to the host. It is
# the single most sensitive artifact this repository's tooling produces - every row is a real
# transaction - so it is untracked, and the ingestion gates ask `git check-ignore` about this path
# before they write the first byte rather than trusting this entry to still be here.
data/store/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# --- REAL Slack credentials found loose in the working tree, 2026-09-02 ---
# `slack-setup.txt` and `whoop-slack-setup.txt` are byte-identical 449-byte notes that hold a live
# `xoxb-` bot token, a live `xapp-` app token, a signing secret and a channel identifier. None of
# the rules above matched them: `.secrets/` needs the leading dot, `ops/env/*.env` needs that path,
# and these two sit at the repository root under ordinary names. This repository is PUBLIC
# (steering §0b), so one `git add -A` would have published production credentials irrecoverably.
# Ignored rather than deleted, for the same reason as the scripts below: they are the owner's own
# handoff notes and a build gate is not a licence to remove them. Their proper home is `.secrets/`
# or a password manager, and per `ops/secrets/ALIAS_REGISTRY.md` a value never belongs in a file
# that git can see at all.
slack-setup.txt
whoop-slack-setup.txt

# Python bytecode and Hypothesis' example database: regenerable caches, never source.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.hypothesis/

# The same keep-awake workstation script family already ignored above, in its timestamped-backup
# and self-test variants (`awake.v3.<date>.bak.ps1`, `awake.tests.ps1`). Identical reasoning to
# `awake.ps1`: one workstation, no importer, no project role, no secret, no deployment particular.
# Committing another person's local pointer-nudging script to a public repository is the worse of
# the two options, and deleting it is not mine to do.
awake.v*.ps1
awake.tests.ps1
